      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبَاعِىٌّ</span></b>  A boy <i>four spans</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْبَار</span>) <i>in height.</i> (S
and Msb voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُمَاسِىٌّ</span>, q. v.) It is also applied to
a camel, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُبَاعِىٌّ</span>; [app. meaning <i>Four cubits
in height</i>:] fem. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>. (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سبع</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
[Also A word <i>composed of four letters, radical
only,</i> or <i>radical and augmentative.</i>]

